// DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE. It ships with s2script and an upgrade OVERWRITES it — any change
// you make here is lost on the next update. To fix or add an entry on a live server, drop a
// .jsonc file in gamedata/cs2/custom/ instead: it is applied last, replaces whole named
// entries, needs no rebuild, and survives upgrades. See docs/INSTALL.md ("Hot-fixing a
// broken signature").
//
// Gamedata master index for the "cs2" owner — the @s2script/cs2 game package's own facts.
// Nothing in shim/src or core/src may name a key in this namespace; that is enforced by
// scripts/check-gamedata-owners.sh.
//
// FILE NAMING follows SourceMod's, deliberately: `master.games.txt` / `common.games.txt` carry the
// owner-level suffix, `engine.csgo.txt` / `game.cstrike.txt` carry the target instead. The mixed
// suffixes are that convention, not an oversight — do not "normalize" them.
{
  "files": [
    { "file": "game.cs2.jsonc", "game": "csgo" }
  ]
}
